      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.praha12.cz/en/index.asp"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The oldest written mention of Modřany dates to 1178 when Duke Sobeslav II granted land to Vysehrad Abbey.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.praha12.cz/en/index.asp"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Modřany’s name likely comes from the blue color of grapes grown there.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.praha12.cz/en/index.asp"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the 1930s functionalist villas appeared as Modřany attracted villa builders.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.praha12.cz/en/index.asp"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Modřany was incorporated into Prague in 1974, ending its status as an independent town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mod%C5%99any"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The sugar refinery in Modřany is one of the oldest in Europe and was the first industrial factory in the area.",
